WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.382 --> 00:00:21.224
Later that day Ally was clearing off a table when she spotted Barry slipping the spring through his

2
00:00:21.264 --> 00:00:21.844
finger again.

3
00:00:21.864 --> 00:00:25.545
"Barry!" she snapped.

4
00:00:25.565 --> 00:00:28.747
"I asked you not to practice at the diner anymore."

5
00:00:28.767 --> 00:00:31.308
"Sorry," he said.

6
00:00:33.144 --> 00:00:37.387
But as soon as Ally turned her back, Barry put a plate of eggs on the spring, tripped,

7
00:00:37.727 --> 00:00:39.328
and spilled eggs all over the floor.

8
00:00:45.593 --> 00:00:47.994
the third plate you've dropped today!

9
00:00:48.795 --> 00:00:51.757
Plus the bowl of cereal that landed on a customer!"

10
00:00:52.337 --> 00:00:56.080
Ally was trying not to get angry, but his tricks were causing problems.

11
00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:00.103
"Go on home.

12
00:01:00.583 --> 00:01:01.404
I'll clean up."

13
00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:07.622
Ally had just finished cleaning up when Mateo arrived.

14
00:01:07.642 --> 00:01:11.745
"Did you find my pod at the museum?"

15
00:01:12.285 --> 00:01:13.286
Ally asked eagerly.

16
00:01:14.807 --> 00:01:16.788
"No." Mateo looked upset.

17
00:01:16.808 --> 00:01:18.869
"I overheard Dr.

18
00:01:18.889 --> 00:01:22.011
Lloyd saying that he hasn't found the ship he lured to Earth yet.

19
00:01:23.432 --> 00:01:25.714
But it's just a matter of time until he does!"

20
00:01:26.755 --> 00:01:27.415
Ally gulped.

21
00:01:29.016 --> 00:01:31.598
"Dr. Lloyd will never give up looking for me!"

22
00:01:31.618 --> 00:01:35.732
"At least we know he doesn't have your ship," Mateo said.

23
00:01:36.733 --> 00:01:38.334
Ally drummed her fingers on the counter.

24
00:01:38.354 --> 00:01:40.375
"But who does?"

25
00:01:40.395 --> 00:01:43.377
"Excuse me."

26
00:01:43.917 --> 00:01:45.498
Randy stuck his head out of the kitchen.

27
00:01:45.518 --> 00:01:47.679
"Is Barry gone?"

28
00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:49.541
When they nodded, he came out.

29
00:01:53.483 --> 00:01:56.485
saw Barry taking pictures of the food delivery today.

30
00:01:56.965 --> 00:01:57.705
It was weird."

31
00:02:01.047 --> 00:02:01.968
He scratched his head.

32
00:02:03.136 --> 00:02:05.037
"I'm worried that kid is up to something."

33
00:02:06.318 --> 00:02:07.939
"Hmm," Mateo said.

34
00:02:07.959 --> 00:02:10.320
"We'll keep an eye on him."

35
00:02:11.441 --> 00:02:13.582
Randy gave a thumbs-up and returned to the kitchen.

36
00:02:17.864 --> 00:02:20.045
keeps causing trouble," Ally said.

37
00:02:20.065 --> 00:02:22.307
"Do you think he knows my secret?"

38
00:02:23.347 --> 00:02:24.848
"No," Mateo said.

39
00:02:24.868 --> 00:02:26.569
"He's just odd."

40
00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:31.592
"When I read his mind, he's always thinking about his dad.

41
00:02:32.136 --> 00:02:33.938
So maybe he's not suspicious of me."

42
00:02:34.698 --> 00:02:35.879
Mateo changed the subject.

43
00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:37.421
"Ready to head home?"

44
00:02:38.201 --> 00:02:39.723
"Yes," Ally said.

45
00:02:39.743 --> 00:02:42.105
"It's been a long day."

46
00:02:44.507 --> 00:02:48.050
After Ally and Mateo left the diner, they walked by the heart sculpture.

47
00:02:48.070 --> 00:02:51.893
"Oh! That reminds me," Ally said.

48
00:02:51.913 --> 00:02:55.777
"I promised the artist that I'd stop by the park to see her work."

49
00:02:55.797 --> 00:02:59.440
"Sounds fun, let's go," Mateo said.

50
00:03:04.568 --> 00:03:07.429
But entering the park reminded Ally of her lost pod again.

51
00:03:07.449 --> 00:03:11.751
"I wish I knew where my pod was," she said.

52
00:03:11.771 --> 00:03:16.313
"And I can't believe I'm saying this, but I really miss Alpha."

53
00:03:16.333 --> 00:03:19.235
"We'll find them," Mateo said.

54
00:03:19.255 --> 00:03:23.136
"Hey, look over there—there's a new sculpture."

55
00:03:24.217 --> 00:03:27.318
He pointed to a large metal ball sitting in the middle of a lawn.

56
00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:31.360
Sarah waved.

57
00:03:34.796 --> 00:03:35.997
"I'm glad you made it.

58
00:03:36.717 --> 00:03:41.720
I know this doesn't look like much yet, but it's going to be a giant model of Earth,

59
00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:43.421
as seen from space."

60
00:03:44.902 --> 00:03:46.203
Ally inspected the ball.

61
00:03:50.225 --> 00:03:53.006
would be cool if you could make it spin on its axis."

62
00:03:53.026 --> 00:03:56.508
"Another great idea!"

63
00:03:56.969 --> 00:03:57.549
Sarah said.

64
00:03:58.609 --> 00:03:59.310
Ally smiled.

65
00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:05.297
"My parents always told me to be helpful Ally stopped when she heard a high-pitched ping.

66
00:04:05.658 --> 00:04:10.260
It was faint, and she wasn't sure where it was coming from, but she'd know that sound anywhere.

67
00:04:11.261 --> 00:04:15.203
Ping ping It was an Astralian distress signal!

68
00:04:15.903 --> 00:04:19.785
As soon as she could, Ally whispered to Mateo to keep Sarah busy for a few minutes.

69
00:04:21.987 --> 00:04:24.608
Then she followed the sound around the metal model of Earth.

70
00:04:26.009 --> 00:04:31.012
On one side of the sculpture, she suddenly spotted something familiar—Astralian symbols.

71
00:04:33.408 --> 00:04:35.610
She stepped closer and let out a startled gasp.

72
00:04:37.612 --> 00:04:42.076
This model of Earth was made from cut-up pieces of metal—from her pod!

73
00:04:42.696 --> 00:04:43.997
Ping ping!

74
00:04:45.198 --> 00:04:48.101
Even worse, that distress signal was coming from Alpha!

75
00:04:48.121 --> 00:04:49.422
"I'm coming, Alpha!"

76
00:04:49.842 --> 00:04:50.443
Ally whispered.

77
00:04:52.345 --> 00:04:56.888
She crawled inside a hole in the huge hollow ball, which was filled with all kinds of junk

78
00:04:56.989 --> 00:04:58.049
and broken technology.

79
00:04:58.069 --> 00:05:00.732
"Where are you?"

80
00:05:03.176 --> 00:05:06.377
Alpha's signal was fading as Ally frantically weeded through the junk.

81
00:05:07.378 --> 00:05:09.859
Then she spotted a motherboard with Astralian symbols.

82
00:05:19.563 --> 00:05:22.044
Ally crawled out of the sculpture, clutching the motherboard.

83
00:05:22.985 --> 00:05:25.266
Sarah beamed when she saw Ally.

84
00:05:33.416 --> 00:05:38.257
"That's exactly what I want kids to do—remove junk from Earth!

85
00:05:38.918 --> 00:05:44.879
You see, my art is a metaphor for how we're polluting our planet, creating mounds of junk.

86
00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:49.180
Oh, and you found the source of that noise too.

87
00:05:49.401 --> 00:05:50.601
Thank goodness!

88
00:05:51.201 --> 00:05:53.422
It's been driving me crazy.

89
00:05:54.262 --> 00:05:56.903
You can keep that object, I mean, if you want it."

90
00:05:58.343 --> 00:06:01.464
"I do want it," Ally said, "very badly!"

91
00:06:02.344 --> 00:06:04.947
Ally and Mateo said good-bye to Sarah and rushed away.

92
00:06:09.091 --> 00:06:10.932
have to hurry, Mateo," Ally said.

93
00:06:10.952 --> 00:06:13.294
"Alpha's signal is fading fast.

94
00:06:13.875 --> 00:06:17.839
If we don't get her connected to a power source soon, we could lose her forever!"
